social impact business are profitable  market-based solutions that address  social needs of low-income populations  in different emerging markets they have  the explicit intention to cause social  impact so the core business is tied to  socially impact and they not only offer  opportunities of employment but mainly  offer products and services that address  the needs of low-income population in  areas such as financial services house  education housing and very important  they need or they should have the  capacity to scale you because as social  problems are very big  we need them to scale  this is a very interesting question in  fact this is a big debate even in the  NGO space so everyone is trying to  measure social impact in the impact  investing field the most common and more  adopted methodology is the gears the  global impact investing rating system a  system that was developed by Jim the  global impact investing Network which is  very good because it's global you can  have a standard so you can compare  businesses from different markets but it  has some limitations the good thing is  they are very open to improvements so  businesses and funds and accelerators  are helping them to improve and this is  a very good standard to be use it it's  very disseminated in Brazil some  businesses have their own indicators  according to their social mission but  the big challenge when you talk about  measuring social impact is when you  think about early-stage business when  entrepreneurs are so busy trying to make  their business be successful that they  don't have time to seek for measurement  so what we really need is a kind of  measurement that is both time and cost  effective to be adopted  also by early-stage entrepreneurs
 

